  "id": "COMPOUND:396 - PROTEIN:932",
  "verbalization": "Loxapine is implicated in the activation of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B (5-HT2B) through a multi-step pathway involving the dopamine D4 receptor and the Alpha-2A adrenergic receptor. The evidence suggests that loxapine acts as a target for multiple receptors, with the dopamine D4 receptor being a direct target of religustilide, which in turn targets the 5-HT2B receptor. Similarly, loxapine itself targets the Alpha-2A adrenergic receptor, which is also a target of religustilide, leading to the same downstream effect on the 5-HT2B receptor. This indicates a potential shared mechanism of action through the activation of these receptors, which may be critical for the therapeutic effects of loxapine. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of receptor targeting in the pharmacological profile of loxapine, with the 5-HT2B receptor serving as a downstream effector in the signaling cascade initiated by loxapine.",
